@startuml
!theme plain
title LCAT (Local Climate Adaptation Tool) - System Architecture

' The system has TWO distinct data flows that meet at the database:
'   * an OFFLINE build pipeline (Sources -> Python) that populates the DB ahead of time (writes)
'   * the RUNTIME request/response path (Database <-> Server <-> Client <-> Browser)
' Each layer is laid out as a compact two-column grid so the image stays roughly
' title-width and the layers stack top to bottom.
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 8
skinparam ranksep 22
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor LightBlue
  BorderColor Blue
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor LightGreen
  BorderColor Green
}
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor LightYellow
  BorderColor Orange
}

' ===== Offline build pipeline (runs ahead of time, writes into the DB) =====
rectangle "Offline build pipeline  ·  run ahead of serving to populate the database" as build_phase #FFF8E1;line:B8860B {

  node "Climate Data Sources" as climate_sources {
    component "CHESS-SCAPE NetCDF files" as chessscape
    component "Boundary shapefiles" as boundaries
    component "Reference data (CSV)" as references
  }

  package "Python Data Pipeline" as python_layer {
    component "**Data Downloaders**\n----\nChessScapeDownloader" as downloaders
    component "**Data Loaders**\n----\nBoundaryLoader\nChessScapeLoader\nChessScapeAveragesLoader\nReferenceLoader\nGridLoader" as loaders
    component "**Data Processors**\n----\nProcessKumu\nProcessReferences\nClimateDataProcessor\nOverlapCalculator\nCoastalIdentifier" as processors
    component "**Analysis Tools**\n----\nDetailsGenerator" as analysis
    component "**DBManager**\n----\nDatabase setup & management" as db_manager
  }
}

' ===== Database (the hub where both flows meet) =====
database "PostgreSQL + PostGIS" as database {
  component "**Climate Data Tables**\n----\nchess_scape_rcp60_*\nchess_scape_rcp85_*\nchess_scape_uk_averages" as climate_tables
  component "**Boundary Tables**\n----\nboundary_uk_counties\nboundary_la_districts\nboundary_lsoa\nboundary_msoa\nboundary_parishes\nboundary_sc_dz\nboundary_ni_dz\nboundary_iom" as boundary_tables
  component "**Reference Tables**\n----\nboundary_details\ngrid_overlaps_*\ncache_*_to_*" as reference_tables
}

' ===== Server (Node.js / Express) — queries the DB at request time =====
package "Server Layer" as server_layer {
  component "**Express App**\n----\nCORS config, static file serving" as app
  component "**API Routes** (rate-limited)\n----\n/api/all_regions\n/api/are_gids_coastal\n/api/region\n/api/gids_bbox\n/api/chess_scape\n/api/chess_scape_uk_averages\n/api/ping" as api
}

' ===== Client (React) =====
package "React Frontend" as client_layer {
  component "**Main App**\n----\nState management, analytics" as main_app
  component "**Climate Components**\n----\nClimateMap, ClimateSettings, ClimateSummary,\nGraph, HelpPopover, ClimatePrediction" as climate_components
  component "**Impact Components**\n----\nClimateHazardRisk, ClimateImpactSummary,\nKumuImpactPathway" as impact_components
  component "**Vulnerability Components**\n----\nPersonalSocialVulnerabilities, IMDMap" as vuln_components
  component "**Adaptation Components**\n----\nStaticAdaptations, StaticAdaptation,\nStaticReferences" as adapt_components
  component "**Utility Components**\n----\nHeader, Footer, Introduction,\nCookieConsent, Feedback" as util_components
  component "**Data Loaders**\n----\nAllRegionLoader, ClimatePredictionLoader,\nClimateAveragesLoader, CoastalFilterLoader,\nGeoJSONLoader" as client_loaders
}

' ===== User browser =====
node "User Browser" as browser {
  component "Interactive map (Leaflet)" as map
  component "Data visualisations (Plotly)" as charts
  component "User interface" as ui
}

' ===== Two-column grid within each layer (keeps it ~title-width) =====
chessscape -[hidden]right-> boundaries
chessscape -[hidden]down-> references

downloaders -[hidden]right-> loaders
processors -[hidden]right-> analysis
downloaders -[hidden]down-> processors
processors -[hidden]down-> db_manager

climate_tables -[hidden]right-> boundary_tables
climate_tables -[hidden]down-> reference_tables

app -[hidden]right-> api

main_app -[hidden]right-> climate_components
impact_components -[hidden]right-> vuln_components
adapt_components -[hidden]right-> util_components
main_app -[hidden]down-> impact_components
impact_components -[hidden]down-> adapt_components
adapt_components -[hidden]down-> client_loaders

map -[hidden]right-> charts
map -[hidden]down-> ui

' ===== Build-time flow: Sources -> Python -> Database (one-way writes, dashed) =====
references -[#B8860B,dashed]down-> downloaders : "ingest"
db_manager -[#B8860B,dashed]down-> climate_tables : "load & write\n(build-time)"

' ===== Runtime flow: request travels down to the DB, response back up (two-way) =====
reference_tables <-down-> api : "SQL queries / results"
api <-down-> main_app : "REST API\nrequest / JSON response"
client_loaders <-down-> map : "render / user interaction"

legend bottom
Two flows meet at the database:
**- - - Offline build pipeline** loads the climate sources into PostgreSQL ahead of serving.
**<-> Runtime path** serves data on demand: Browser <-> React <-> Express API <-> Database.
====
**Technology stack** — Frontend: React, Leaflet, Plotly | Backend: Node.js, Express | Database: PostgreSQL + PostGIS | Data pipeline: Python, NetCDF, GeoPandas
endlegend

@enduml
